I wrote the session plan: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored. The instruction's || true suggests that's expected and the harness reads the files from disk, but I haven't confirmed that.

Task 1 — Fixes #1123, Part of #1124 and #1122 (product). This is the creator's ask on #1122: delete the two Day-247 stopgaps now that yoagent 0.26.7 is in the lock.
• The hand-written Sonnet 4.6 row becomes ModelConfig::claude_sonnet_4_6(). Before deleting, the implementer compares the old row and yoagent's field by field and writes any difference into the commit.
• Bedrock limits come from ModelConfig::preset("bedrock", id). Only the limit and reasoning fields are copied over, never base_url or cost.
• The two resolvers don't accept the same ids: yoyo's takes any lowercase region prefix, yoagent's takes 9 named ones. The task measures where they disagree, row by row. yoagent becomes the authority, and any real AWS id it refuses gets filed upstream.
• providers::bedrock_anthropic_preset_id stays for now, as a pricing-only lookup. yoagent's Bedrock preset has no price and doesn't keep the Anthropic model id, and bedrock_region.rs needs that id to price Bedrock in /cost. So #1124 stays open for the pricing half.

Task 2 — Fixes #1129 (product, backlog drain). There are 17 open self-filed issues, over the limit of 12, and this one has the least work left. yoyo review gets its own flag list in verb_flags, the same way the seven sibling verbs did in 78a31e61. A mistyped flag like --quik or --thorogh will be refused with exit 2 and a did-you-mean suggestion. --print will no longer be read as a PR number, because --pr is no longer matched by prefix. The task also lists the inputs whose behaviour must not change.

Other decisions:
• Neither task touches prompt (the trajectory flagged it at 5 of the last 10 diffs) or config.rs, which is 11 lines from the size-gate failure point.
• No release: it isn't due (14 days, 51 commits since v0.3.0).
• #1121, #1117, #1127, #1128, #1126 and #1114 are deferred, with responses in issue_responses.md.
